  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Human insulin is an anti-diabetic medication used to treat type-1 diabetes and maturity-onset diabetes of the young type 2. It is widely used and remains authorised in the European Union for diabetes, available in fast-acting, intermediate-acting, long-acting, combined, and inhaled forms.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q50265665\">Wikidata Q50265665</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>insulin (human)</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>A10AB01, A10AB01;A10AC01, A10AC01, A10AD01, A10AE01, A10AF01</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=\"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB00030\">DB00030</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:5931\">5931</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q50265665\">Q50265665</a></td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>5808 g/mol (Drugs.Common 25.09, not verified)</td></tr><tr><td>logP:</td><td>-13.1 (Drugs.Common 25.09, not verified)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
